@page
@model CheatSheetModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Cheat sheet";
}

@*
    The printable sheet (D120). Everything here is rendered server side in one go — no htmx, no
    polling, no table plugin — because a sheet that is about to become paper has nothing to
    refresh. The print styling is two things and no more: Bootstrap's own d-print-none on the
    button and on the layout's navbar and footer, and the @@media print block in site.css that
    forces light colours so dark mode does not print white text on white paper.
*@
<div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start mb-3">
    <div>
        <h1 class="h3 mb-1">Phone cheat sheet</h1>
        <p class="text-body-secondary mb-0">@Model.SiteName &middot; @Model.PrintedOn</p>
    </div>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary d-print-none" onclick="window.print()">Print</button>
</div>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Extensions</h2>
@if (Model.Numbers.Count == 0)
{
    <p class="text-body-secondary">No extensions yet.</p>
}
else
{
    <table class="table table-sm table-bordered align-middle">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th scope="col" style="width: 6rem;">Number</th>
                <th scope="col">Name</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var extension in Model.Numbers)
            {
                <tr>
                    <td class="fw-bold">@extension.Number</td>
                    <td>@extension.Name</td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
}

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Codes you can dial</h2>
<table class="table table-sm table-bordered align-middle">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th scope="col" style="width: 6rem;">Press</th>
            <th scope="col" style="width: 14rem;">What it is</th>
            <th scope="col">What happens</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        @* Grouped in the order FeatureCodes.All builds them: what works mid-call first, then
           what you dial instead of a call. A group with nothing in it never appears, because a
           code that is switched off is never in the list to begin with. *@
        @* "part" rather than "section" or "group": @@section is a Razor directive and would be
           parsed as one here. *@
        @foreach (var part in Model.Codes.GroupBy(c => c.Group))
        {
            <tr>
                <th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">@part.Key</th>
            </tr>

            @foreach (var entry in part)
            {
                <tr>
                    <td class="fw-bold">@entry.Code</td>
                    <td>@entry.Name</td>
                    <td>@entry.Description</td>
                </tr>
            }
        }
    </tbody>
</table>
